<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lord Meng of Huang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lord Meng of Huang was a ruler of the small Zhou-era state of Huang in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> in the 7th century BCE. His tomb and that of his wife were excavated at Guangshan in 1983 and yielded fine bronze vessels, jades and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lacquerware">lacquerware</a>, which show an aristocratic culture close to that of the Central Plain. Huang was destroyed by the State of Chu in 648 BCE.</p></div>
